[2026-03-14T20:31:48.423Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JzzrmWG1FGKgoiX3oAasLn","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile a comprehensive report.\n\n## Comprehensive Google Flights App Exploration Report\n\n### 1. APP DIRECTORY AND STRUCTURE\n\n**App Directory Name:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights`\n\n**Directory Structure:**\n```\n/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/\n├── src/\n│   ├── components/          (32 component files including TripCard, TrackedRouteCard, CancelBookingModal)\n│   ├── pages/               (5 page files: SearchPage, SearchResultsPage, ExplorePage, FlightDetailsPage, MyTripsPage)\n│   ├── slices/              (5 Redux slices: bookingSlice, exploreSlice, flightsSlice, searchSlice, tripsSlice)\n│   ├── main.tsx\n│   ├── store.ts\n│   ├── vite-env.d.ts\n│   └── App.tsx\n├── tests/                   (21 .spec.ts files)\n├── netlify/\n│   └── functions/           (12 serverless functions)\n├── scripts/\n│   └── seed-db.ts\n├── docs/\n│   └── tests.md            (1413 lines of test specifications)\n├── playwright.config.ts\n└── dist/, node_modules/, logs/\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. DOCS/TESTS.MD CONTENT\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/docs/tests.md` (1413 lines)\n\nThis is a comprehensive test specification document covering:\n- **Search Page Components:** TripTypeSelector, PassengerCountSelector, CabinClassSelector, AirportAutocomplete, DatePicker, SearchButton, RecentSearches, PopularDestinations\n- **Search Results Page:** FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard, Pagination, SearchSummaryBar, TrackPricesToggle\n- **Flight Details & Booking:** FlightSummary, BookingAction, PassengerForm, PriceBreakdown\n- **My Trips Page:** TripsTabs, TripCard, TrackedRouteCard, CancelBookingModal\n\nThe document provides detailed test cases for each component including:\n- Initial state requirements\n- User interactions\n- Expected outputs\n- Edge cases and special conditions\n\n---\n\n### 3. COMPONENT FILES: TRIPCARD, TRACKEDROUTECARD, CANCELBOOKINGMODAL\n\n#### **TripCard.tsx** (`/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/TripCard.tsx`)\n\n**Purpose:** Displays a single booking/trip with all its details\n\n**Props:**\n```typescript\ninterface TripCardProps {\n  booking: BookingTrip\n  showCancelButton: boolean\n  onCancel?: (booking: BookingTrip) => void\n}\n```\n\n**Key data-testid values:**\n- `trip-card-${booking.id}` - Main card container\n- `trip-card-airline-logo-${booking.id}` - Airline logo circle\n- `trip-card-status-${booking.id}` - Status badge (Confirmed/Completed/Cancelled)\n- `trip-card-route-${booking.id}` - Route text (e.g., \"LAX → JFK\")\n- `trip-card-dates-${booking.id}` - Departure and optional return dates\n- `trip-card-price-${booking.id}` - Total price formatted as \"$###.##\"\n- `trip-card-ref-${booking.id}` - Booking reference (e.g., \"GF-ABC123\")\n- `trip-card-cancel-${booking.id}` - Cancel button (only shown if showCancelButton=true and status='confirmed')\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Displays airline logo with background color from `booking.logo_color`\n- Shows airline name and flight number\n- Displays route with IATA codes and arrow separator\n- Shows both departure and return dates for round trips\n- Formats prices from cents to dollar format\n- Status badge with CSS class based on status: `trip-card__status--confirmed`, `trip-card__status--completed`, `trip-card__status--cancelled`\n- Cancel button only appears for confirmed upcoming trips\n\n---\n\n#### **TrackedRouteCard.tsx** (`/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/TrackedRouteCard.tsx`)\n\n**Purpose:** Displays a tracked price route that user is monitoring\n\n**Props:**\n```typescript\ninterface TrackedRouteCardProps {\n  route: TrackedRoute\n  onUntrack: (routeId: string) => void\n  isUntracking: boolean\n}\n```\n\n**Key data-testid values:**\n- `tracked-route-card-${route.id}` - Main card container\n- `tracked-route-route-${route.id}` - Route text (e.g., \"LAX → JFK\")\n- `tracked-route-dates-${route.id}` - Date range display (with calendar icon)\n- `tracked-route-price-${route.id}` - Lowest price section\n- `tracked-route-search-${route.id}` - \"Search\" button\n- `tracked-route-untrack-${route.id}` - \"Untrack\" button (shows \"Removing...\" when disabled)\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Displays route with origin/destination codes and city names\n- Shows flexible date range or \"Any dates\" if no dates specified\n- Displays lowest price found in green\n- Two action buttons: \"Search\" (navigates to results page) and \"Untrack\" (deletes tracking)\n- Button text changes to \"Removing...\" during untrack operation\n- Uses calendar icon SVG inline\n\n---\n\n#### **CancelBookingModal.tsx** (`/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/CancelBookingModal.tsx`)\n\n**Purpose:** Modal dialog to confirm cancellation of a booking\n\n**Props:**\n```typescript\ninterface CancelBookingModalProps {\n  booking: BookingTrip\n  onConfirm: () => void\n  onDismiss: () => void\n  isCancelling: boolean\n  error: string | null\n}\n```\n\n**Key data-testid values:**\n- `cancel-modal-overlay` - Overlay backdrop (clickable to dismiss)\n- `cancel-booking-modal` - Modal container\n- `cancel-modal-details` - Details section containing booking info\n- `cancel-modal-error` - Error message display (only shown if error is truthy)\n- `cancel-modal-keep` - \"Keep Booking\" button (dismiss button)\n- `cancel-modal-confirm` - \"Cancel Booking\" button (confirm button)\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Fixed overlay with semi-transparent background\n- Modal can be dismissed by:\n  - Clicking overlay (outside modal)\n  - Pressing Escape key\n  - Clicking \"Keep Booking\" button\n- Displays booking details in a details section:\n  - Route (origin_code → dest_code)\n  - Date (formatted as \"Mon ##\")\n  - Flight (airline_name flight_number)\n  - Reference (booking_reference, in monospace font)\n- Error message displayed in red background if present\n- Both buttons disabled during cancellation (isCancelling=true)\n- \"Cancel Booking\" button shows \"Cancelling...\" text while in progress\n- Uses event.stopPropagation() to prevent modal from closing when clicking inside\n\n---\n\n### 4. EXISTING TEST FILES (*.spec.ts)\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/tests/`\n\n**Available Test Files (21 total):**\n- airport-autocomplete.spec.ts\n- booking-action.spec.ts\n- cabin-class-selector.spec.ts\n- date-picker.spec.ts\n- filter-sidebar.spec.ts\n- filter-sidebar-combined.spec.ts\n- flight-result-card.spec.ts\n- flight-summary.spec.ts\n- pagination.spec.ts\n- passenger-count-selector.spec.ts\n- passenger-form.spec.ts\n- popular-destinations.spec.ts\n- price-breakdown.spec.ts\n- recent-searches.spec.ts\n- search-button.spec.ts\n- search-summary-bar.spec.ts\n- **track-prices-toggle.spec.ts** (tests tracking functionality)\n- trip-type-selector.spec.ts\n- **trip-card.spec.ts** (existing comprehensive test suite)\n- **trips-tabs.spec.ts** (tab switching tests)\n\n**TripCard Test Suite** (`/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/tests/trip-card.spec.ts` - 244 lines):\n- Tests route information display\n- Tests travel dates display (including round-trip date ranges)\n- Tests airline and flight info display\n- Tests status badges (Confirmed, Completed, Cancelled)\n- Tests price display\n- Tests booking reference display\n- Tests cancel button visibility (only for upcoming confirmed flights)\n- Tests one-way trip display\n- Uses helper function `findTripCardByRef()` to locate cards by booking reference within a list\n\n---\n\n### 5. PLAYWRIGHT.CONFIG.TS\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/playwright.config.ts`\n\n**Configuration Details:**\n- **Test Directory:** `./tests`\n- **Timeout:** 60,000ms (1 minute)\n- **Expect Timeout:** 10,000ms\n- **Parallelization:** Disabled (`fullyParallel: false`, `workers: 1`)\n- **Retries:** 0\n- **Reporters:** List and JSON (outputs to `test-results/results.json`)\n- **Base URL:** `http://localhost:8888`\n- **Browser:** Chromium with Replay.io executable path\n- **Trace:** Recorded on first retry\n- **Web Server:** Netlify dev server on port 8888 with functions from `./netlify/functions`\n- **Server Reuse:** Enabled in non-CI environments\n\n---\n\n### 6. SEED DATA FILE\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/seed-db.ts` (407 lines)\n\n**Seed Data Includes:**\n\n**Airports:** 50 major international airports (LAX, JFK, SFO, LHR, CDG, DXB, SIN, NRT, HKG, SYD, MEL, etc.)\n\n**Airlines:** 20 airlines with IATA codes and logo colors:\n- AA (American Airlines, #E31837)\n- DL (Delta Air Lines, #003366)\n- UA (United Airlines, #002244)\n- WN (Southwest Airlines, #F9A01B)\n- And 16 others including international carriers\n\n**Flights:** ~200 flights with realistic routes, times, aircraft types, and amenities\n\n**Sample Bookings (for testing):**\n1. **GF-ABC123** - LAX→JFK, Apr 1, AA100, economy, $343.85, **confirmed** (upcoming)\n2. **GF-PAST01** - LAX→JFK, Feb 1, DL950, economy, $286.35, **completed** (past)\n3. **GF-CANC01** - LAX→JFK, Apr 1, DL200, economy, $320.85, **cancelled** (upcoming)\n4. **GF-SORT01** - LAX→JFK (Mar 25) + JFK→LAX return (Mar 30), AA960+AA965, economy, $332.35, **confirmed** (round trip)\n5. **GF-SORT02** - LAX→JFK, Mar 30, DL960, economy, $309.35, **confirmed**\n6. **GF-SORT03** - LAX→JFK, Apr 10, UA970, economy, $355.35, **confirmed**\n7. **GF-ONEW01** - SFO→ORD, Apr 5, AA970, economy, $205.85, **confirmed** (one-way)\n\n**Tracked Routes:**\n- LAX → LHR, dates Apr 15-30, economy cabin\n\n**Session:** `seed-session-token` used for testing\n\n---\n\n### 7. NETLIFY FUNCTIONS HANDLING TRIPS, TRACKED ROUTES, AND BOOKINGS\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify/functions/`\n\n#### **bookings.ts** (175 lines)\n- **POST:** Create new booking\n  - Accepts: sessionToken, flightId, returnFlightId, cabinClass, totalPriceCents, passengers array\n  - Generates random booking reference (format: \"GF-XXXXXX\")\n  - Creates or uses existing session\n  - Inserts passenger data\n  - Returns: booking id, reference, status, createdAt\n- **GET:** Fetch flight details for booking page\n  - Accepts: flightId, cabinClass\n  - Returns: flight details with pricing and leg information\n\n#### **my-bookings.ts** (101 lines)\n- **GET:** Fetch all bookings for a session\n  - Accepts: session (query param)\n  - Returns: Array of BookingTrip objects with flight, airline, airport info\n  - Includes: return_flight_id, return_departure_time, return_arrival_time\n  - Orders by departure_time ascending\n- **PATCH:** Cancel a booking\n  - Accepts: bookingId, sessionToken, status ('cancelled')\n  - Only allows cancelling from 'confirmed' status\n  - Returns: Updated booking id and status\n\n#### **tracked-routes.ts** (127 lines)\n- **GET:** Fetch all tracked routes for a session OR check if specific route is tracked\n  - With origin & destination params: Returns `{ tracked: boolean, id: string|null }`\n  - Without route params: Returns array of TrackedRoute objects with lowest_price_cents\n  - Orders by created_at DESC\n- **POST:** Track a new route\n  - Accepts: sessionToken, originCode, destCode, departureDateStart, departureDateEnd, cabinClass\n  - Creates session if needed\n  - Returns: `{ success: true }`\n- **DELETE:** Untrack a route\n  - Can delete by id OR by originCode + destCode\n  - Returns: `{ success: true }`\n\n---\n\n### 8. SHARED MODAL/DIALOG COMPONENTS\n\n**Found Components:**\n\n**CancelBookingModal** (only modal component found)\n- Located: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/CancelBookingModal.tsx`\n- CSS: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/CancelBookingModal.css`\n- Uses: Fixed overlay with z-index: 1000\n- Keyboard support: Escape key closes modal\n- Click outside: Clicking overlay dismisses modal\n- No additional shared modal utilities found\n\n**Note:** The app does NOT use a shared modal library or utility. CancelBookingModal is a standalone component with its own styling and behavior implementation.\n\n---\n\n### SUMMARY OF KEY DATA-TESTID VALUES\n\n**TripCard Test IDs Pattern:**\n- Container: `trip-card-{id}`\n- Airline Logo: `trip-card-airline-logo-{id}`\n- Status: `trip-card-status-{id}`\n- Route: `trip-card-route-{id}`\n- Dates: `trip-card-dates-{id}`\n- Price: `trip-card-price-{id}`\n- Reference: `trip-card-ref-{id}`\n- Cancel Button: `trip-card-cancel-{id}`\n\n**TrackedRouteCard Test IDs Pattern:**\n- Container: `tracked-route-card-{id}`\n- Route: `tracked-route-route-{id}`\n- Dates: `tracked-route-dates-{id}`\n- Price: `tracked-route-price-{id}`\n- Search Button: `tracked-route-search-{id}`\n- Untrack Button: `tracked-route-untrack-{id}`\n\n**CancelBookingModal Test IDs (fixed):**\n- Overlay: `cancel-modal-overlay`\n- Modal: `cancel-booking-modal`\n- Details Section: `cancel-modal-details`\n- Error: `cancel-modal-error`\n- Keep Button: `cancel-modal-keep`\n- Confirm Button: `cancel-modal-confirm`\n\n**Trip List Test IDs:**\n- Upcoming list: `trips-upcoming-list`\n- Past list: `trips-past-list`\n- Tracked list: `trips-tracked-list`\n- Tabs: `trips-tab-upcoming`, `trips-tab-past`, `trips-tab-tracked`\n\n---\n\nAll absolute file paths are now available for reference in your testing work."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a05b184f4aa381f33 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 71400\ntool_uses: 35\nduration_ms: 63797</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69f9b163-3df5-4d89-bb17-117162edeb04","uuid":"a9f36b25-b1e1-4c82-8e1e-c79d0e026b13","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the google-flights app in /repo/apps/. Find:\n1. The app directory name and structure\n2. The docs/tests.md file content\n3. All component files related to TripCard, TrackedRouteCard, and CancelBookingModal\n4. Any existing test files (*.spec.ts)\n5. The playwright.config.ts\n6. The seed data file\n7. The netlify functions that handle trips, tracked routes, and bookings\n8. Any shared modal/dialog components\n\nBe very thorough - read the actual component source code for TripCard, TrackedRouteCard, and CancelBookingModal so we know the exact data-testid values and structure.","agentId":"a05b184f4aa381f33","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile a comprehensive report.\n\n## Comprehensive Google Flights App Exploration Report\n\n### 1. APP DIRECTORY AND STRUCTURE\n\n**App Directory Name:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights`\n\n**Directory Structure:**\n```\n/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/\n├── src/\n│   ├── components/          (32 component files including TripCard, TrackedRouteCard, CancelBookingModal)\n│   ├── pages/               (5 page files: SearchPage, SearchResultsPage, ExplorePage, FlightDetailsPage, MyTripsPage)\n│   ├── slices/              (5 Redux slices: bookingSlice, exploreSlice, flightsSlice, searchSlice, tripsSlice)\n│   ├── main.tsx\n│   ├── store.ts\n│   ├── vite-env.d.ts\n│   └── App.tsx\n├── tests/                   (21 .spec.ts files)\n├── netlify/\n│   └── functions/           (12 serverless functions)\n├── scripts/\n│   └── seed-db.ts\n├── docs/\n│   └── tests.md            (1413 lines of test specifications)\n├── playwright.config.ts\n└── dist/, node_modules/, logs/\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. DOCS/TESTS.MD CONTENT\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/docs/tests.md` (1413 lines)\n\nThis is a comprehensive test specification document covering:\n- **Search Page Components:** TripTypeSelector, PassengerCountSelector, CabinClassSelector, AirportAutocomplete, DatePicker, SearchButton, RecentSearches, PopularDestinations\n- **Search Results Page:** FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard, Pagination, SearchSummaryBar, TrackPricesToggle\n- **Flight Details & Booking:** FlightSummary, BookingAction, PassengerForm, PriceBreakdown\n- **My Trips Page:** TripsTabs, TripCard, TrackedRouteCard, CancelBookingModal\n\nThe document provides detailed test cases for each component including:\n- Initial state requirements\n- User interactions\n- Expected outputs\n- Edge cases and special conditions\n\n---\n\n### 3. COMPONENT FILES: TRIPCARD, TRACKEDROUTECARD, CANCELBOOKINGMODAL\n\n#### **TripCard.tsx** (`/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/TripCard.tsx`)\n\n**Purpose:** Displays a single booking/trip with all its details\n\n**Props:**\n```typescript\ninterface TripCardProps {\n  booking: BookingTrip\n  showCancelButton: boolean\n  onCancel?: (booking: BookingTrip) => void\n}\n```\n\n**Key data-testid values:**\n- `trip-card-${booking.id}` - Main card container\n- `trip-card-airline-logo-${booking.id}` - Airline logo circle\n- `trip-card-status-${booking.id}` - Status badge (Confirmed/Completed/Cancelled)\n- `trip-card-route-${booking.id}` - Route text (e.g., \"LAX → JFK\")\n- `trip-card-dates-${booking.id}` - Departure and optional return dates\n- `trip-card-price-${booking.id}` - Total price formatted as \"$###.##\"\n- `trip-card-ref-${booking.id}` - Booking reference (e.g., \"GF-ABC123\")\n- `trip-card-cancel-${booking.id}` - Cancel button (only shown if showCancelButton=true and status='confirmed')\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Displays airline logo with background color from `booking.logo_color`\n- Shows airline name and flight number\n- Displays route with IATA codes and arrow separator\n- Shows both departure and return dates for round trips\n- Formats prices from cents to dollar format\n- Status badge with CSS class based on status: `trip-card__status--confirmed`, `trip-card__status--completed`, `trip-card__status--cancelled`\n- Cancel button only appears for confirmed upcoming trips\n\n---\n\n#### **TrackedRouteCard.tsx** (`/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/TrackedRouteCard.tsx`)\n\n**Purpose:** Displays a tracked price route that user is monitoring\n\n**Props:**\n```typescript\ninterface TrackedRouteCardProps {\n  route: TrackedRoute\n  onUntrack: (routeId: string) => void\n  isUntracking: boolean\n}\n```\n\n**Key data-testid values:**\n- `tracked-route-card-${route.id}` - Main card container\n- `tracked-route-route-${route.id}` - Route text (e.g., \"LAX → JFK\")\n- `tracked-route-dates-${route.id}` - Date range display (with calendar icon)\n- `tracked-route-price-${route.id}` - Lowest price section\n- `tracked-route-search-${route.id}` - \"Search\" button\n- `tracked-route-untrack-${route.id}` - \"Untrack\" button (shows \"Removing...\" when disabled)\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Displays route with origin/destination codes and city names\n- Shows flexible date range or \"Any dates\" if no dates specified\n- Displays lowest price found in green\n- Two action buttons: \"Search\" (navigates to results page) and \"Untrack\" (deletes tracking)\n- Button text changes to \"Removing...\" during untrack operation\n- Uses calendar icon SVG inline\n\n---\n\n#### **CancelBookingModal.tsx** (`/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/CancelBookingModal.tsx`)\n\n**Purpose:** Modal dialog to confirm cancellation of a booking\n\n**Props:**\n```typescript\ninterface CancelBookingModalProps {\n  booking: BookingTrip\n  onConfirm: () => void\n  onDismiss: () => void\n  isCancelling: boolean\n  error: string | null\n}\n```\n\n**Key data-testid values:**\n- `cancel-modal-overlay` - Overlay backdrop (clickable to dismiss)\n- `cancel-booking-modal` - Modal container\n- `cancel-modal-details` - Details section containing booking info\n- `cancel-modal-error` - Error message display (only shown if error is truthy)\n- `cancel-modal-keep` - \"Keep Booking\" button (dismiss button)\n- `cancel-modal-confirm` - \"Cancel Booking\" button (confirm button)\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Fixed overlay with semi-transparent background\n- Modal can be dismissed by:\n  - Clicking overlay (outside modal)\n  - Pressing Escape key\n  - Clicking \"Keep Booking\" button\n- Displays booking details in a details section:\n  - Route (origin_code → dest_code)\n  - Date (formatted as \"Mon ##\")\n  - Flight (airline_name flight_number)\n  - Reference (booking_reference, in monospace font)\n- Error message displayed in red background if present\n- Both buttons disabled during cancellation (isCancelling=true)\n- \"Cancel Booking\" button shows \"Cancelling...\" text while in progress\n- Uses event.stopPropagation() to prevent modal from closing when clicking inside\n\n---\n\n### 4. EXISTING TEST FILES (*.spec.ts)\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/tests/`\n\n**Available Test Files (21 total):**\n- airport-autocomplete.spec.ts\n- booking-action.spec.ts\n- cabin-class-selector.spec.ts\n- date-picker.spec.ts\n- filter-sidebar.spec.ts\n- filter-sidebar-combined.spec.ts\n- flight-result-card.spec.ts\n- flight-summary.spec.ts\n- pagination.spec.ts\n- passenger-count-selector.spec.ts\n- passenger-form.spec.ts\n- popular-destinations.spec.ts\n- price-breakdown.spec.ts\n- recent-searches.spec.ts\n- search-button.spec.ts\n- search-summary-bar.spec.ts\n- **track-prices-toggle.spec.ts** (tests tracking functionality)\n- trip-type-selector.spec.ts\n- **trip-card.spec.ts** (existing comprehensive test suite)\n- **trips-tabs.spec.ts** (tab switching tests)\n\n**TripCard Test Suite** (`/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/tests/trip-card.spec.ts` - 244 lines):\n- Tests route information display\n- Tests travel dates display (including round-trip date ranges)\n- Tests airline and flight info display\n- Tests status badges (Confirmed, Completed, Cancelled)\n- Tests price display\n- Tests booking reference display\n- Tests cancel button visibility (only for upcoming confirmed flights)\n- Tests one-way trip display\n- Uses helper function `findTripCardByRef()` to locate cards by booking reference within a list\n\n---\n\n### 5. PLAYWRIGHT.CONFIG.TS\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/playwright.config.ts`\n\n**Configuration Details:**\n- **Test Directory:** `./tests`\n- **Timeout:** 60,000ms (1 minute)\n- **Expect Timeout:** 10,000ms\n- **Parallelization:** Disabled (`fullyParallel: false`, `workers: 1`)\n- **Retries:** 0\n- **Reporters:** List and JSON (outputs to `test-results/results.json`)\n- **Base URL:** `http://localhost:8888`\n- **Browser:** Chromium with Replay.io executable path\n- **Trace:** Recorded on first retry\n- **Web Server:** Netlify dev server on port 8888 with functions from `./netlify/functions`\n- **Server Reuse:** Enabled in non-CI environments\n\n---\n\n### 6. SEED DATA FILE\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/seed-db.ts` (407 lines)\n\n**Seed Data Includes:**\n\n**Airports:** 50 major international airports (LAX, JFK, SFO, LHR, CDG, DXB, SIN, NRT, HKG, SYD, MEL, etc.)\n\n**Airlines:** 20 airlines with IATA codes and logo colors:\n- AA (American Airlines, #E31837)\n- DL (Delta Air Lines, #003366)\n- UA (United Airlines, #002244)\n- WN (Southwest Airlines, #F9A01B)\n- And 16 others including international carriers\n\n**Flights:** ~200 flights with realistic routes, times, aircraft types, and amenities\n\n**Sample Bookings (for testing):**\n1. **GF-ABC123** - LAX→JFK, Apr 1, AA100, economy, $343.85, **confirmed** (upcoming)\n2. **GF-PAST01** - LAX→JFK, Feb 1, DL950, economy, $286.35, **completed** (past)\n3. **GF-CANC01** - LAX→JFK, Apr 1, DL200, economy, $320.85, **cancelled** (upcoming)\n4. **GF-SORT01** - LAX→JFK (Mar 25) + JFK→LAX return (Mar 30), AA960+AA965, economy, $332.35, **confirmed** (round trip)\n5. **GF-SORT02** - LAX→JFK, Mar 30, DL960, economy, $309.35, **confirmed**\n6. **GF-SORT03** - LAX→JFK, Apr 10, UA970, economy, $355.35, **confirmed**\n7. **GF-ONEW01** - SFO→ORD, Apr 5, AA970, economy, $205.85, **confirmed** (one-way)\n\n**Tracked Routes:**\n- LAX → LHR, dates Apr 15-30, economy cabin\n\n**Session:** `seed-session-token` used for testing\n\n---\n\n### 7. NETLIFY FUNCTIONS HANDLING TRIPS, TRACKED ROUTES, AND BOOKINGS\n\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify/functions/`\n\n#### **bookings.ts** (175 lines)\n- **POST:** Create new booking\n  - Accepts: sessionToken, flightId, returnFlightId, cabinClass, totalPriceCents, passengers array\n  - Generates random booking reference (format: \"GF-XXXXXX\")\n  - Creates or uses existing session\n  - Inserts passenger data\n  - Returns: booking id, reference, status, createdAt\n- **GET:** Fetch flight details for booking page\n  - Accepts: flightId, cabinClass\n  - Returns: flight details with pricing and leg information\n\n#### **my-bookings.ts** (101 lines)\n- **GET:** Fetch all bookings for a session\n  - Accepts: session (query param)\n  - Returns: Array of BookingTrip objects with flight, airline, airport info\n  - Includes: return_flight_id, return_departure_time, return_arrival_time\n  - Orders by departure_time ascending\n- **PATCH:** Cancel a booking\n  - Accepts: bookingId, sessionToken, status ('cancelled')\n  - Only allows cancelling from 'confirmed' status\n  - Returns: Updated booking id and status\n\n#### **tracked-routes.ts** (127 lines)\n- **GET:** Fetch all tracked routes for a session OR check if specific route is tracked\n  - With origin & destination params: Returns `{ tracked: boolean, id: string|null }`\n  - Without route params: Returns array of TrackedRoute objects with lowest_price_cents\n  - Orders by created_at DESC\n- **POST:** Track a new route\n  - Accepts: sessionToken, originCode, destCode, departureDateStart, departureDateEnd, cabinClass\n  - Creates session if needed\n  - Returns: `{ success: true }`\n- **DELETE:** Untrack a route\n  - Can delete by id OR by originCode + destCode\n  - Returns: `{ success: true }`\n\n---\n\n### 8. SHARED MODAL/DIALOG COMPONENTS\n\n**Found Components:**\n\n**CancelBookingModal** (only modal component found)\n- Located: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/CancelBookingModal.tsx`\n- CSS: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/CancelBookingModal.css`\n- Uses: Fixed overlay with z-index: 1000\n- Keyboard support: Escape key closes modal\n- Click outside: Clicking overlay dismisses modal\n- No additional shared modal utilities found\n\n**Note:** The app does NOT use a shared modal library or utility. CancelBookingModal is a standalone component with its own styling and behavior implementation.\n\n---\n\n### SUMMARY OF KEY DATA-TESTID VALUES\n\n**TripCard Test IDs Pattern:**\n- Container: `trip-card-{id}`\n- Airline Logo: `trip-card-airline-logo-{id}`\n- Status: `trip-card-status-{id}`\n- Route: `trip-card-route-{id}`\n- Dates: `trip-card-dates-{id}`\n- Price: `trip-card-price-{id}`\n- Reference: `trip-card-ref-{id}`\n- Cancel Button: `trip-card-cancel-{id}`\n\n**TrackedRouteCard Test IDs Pattern:**\n- Container: `tracked-route-card-{id}`\n- Route: `tracked-route-route-{id}`\n- Dates: `tracked-route-dates-{id}`\n- Price: `tracked-route-price-{id}`\n- Search Button: `tracked-route-search-{id}`\n- Untrack Button: `tracked-route-untrack-{id}`\n\n**CancelBookingModal Test IDs (fixed):**\n- Overlay: `cancel-modal-overlay`\n- Modal: `cancel-booking-modal`\n- Details Section: `cancel-modal-details`\n- Error: `cancel-modal-error`\n- Keep Button: `cancel-modal-keep`\n- Confirm Button: `cancel-modal-confirm`\n\n**Trip List Test IDs:**\n- Upcoming list: `trips-upcoming-list`\n- Past list: `trips-past-list`\n- Tracked list: `trips-tracked-list`\n- Tabs: `trips-tab-upcoming`, `trips-tab-past`, `trips-tab-tracked`\n\n---\n\nAll absolute file paths are now available for reference in your testing work."}],"totalDurationMs":63797,"totalTokens":71400,"totalToolUseCount":35,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4316,"cache_read_input_tokens":63119,"output_tokens":3959,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4316},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
